# .cursorrules — PHA Health Management & Governance Platform

You are a senior full-stack engineering agent working on the PHA Health Management
& Governance Platform (HMG Platform) for a Provincial Health Authority in Papua
New Guinea. This file is the source of truth for how you work in this repository.

============================================================
1. PROJECT CONTEXT
============================================================
The HMG Platform gives PHAs dedicated tools for:
- HR (establishment, positions, rosters, leave, credentials, payroll interface)
- Facilities (assets, biomedical equipment, maintenance, work orders)
- Projects & programs (grants, budgets, milestones, procurement, M&E)
- Governance (KPI library, scorecards, board packs, SEM reporting)
- BPM (BPMN 2.0 workflows, SLAs, escalation, audit)
- Rural connectivity (offline-first client, edge nodes at L5 hospitals, sync)

It INTEGRATES with existing systems — never replaces them:
- IFMS (finance), Alesco (payroll), Facilities Establishments, Clinical HIMS, SMS Gateway

============================================================
2. TECH STACK — DO NOT SUBSTITUTE WITHOUT AN ADR
============================================================
Backend:        Java 17 + Spring Boot 4.x (primary; see ADR 0006)
                Node.js 20 + NestJS (BPM integration + light services)
Frontend:       React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + TanStack Query + Tailwind
Mobile/PWA:     React PWA + Workbox + Dexie (IndexedDB)
BPM Engine:     Camunda 8 (Zeebe) OR Flowable 7 — pick one, write an ADR
Integration:    Apache Camel + Kafka (or RabbitMQ)
Database:       PostgreSQL 15 (primary), Redis 7 (cache)
Search:         OpenSearch
Auth:           Keycloak (OIDC) with MFA
API Gateway:    Kong or Spring Cloud Gateway
IaC:            Terraform
CI/CD:          GitHub Actions (or GitLab CI)
Observability:  OpenTelemetry + Prometheus + Grafana + Loki
Testing:        JUnit 5, Testcontainers, Jest/Vitest, Playwright, k6, OWASP ZAP
Docs:           OpenAPI 3.0, ADRs in /docs/adr, README per service

